Package: lindos-compat
Version: 1.0.0
Section: otherosfs
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), lindos-core (>= 1.0.0), cabextract, winbind, xdg-utils, desktop-file-utils, shared-mime-info
Recommends: winehq-staging | wine-staging | wine, winetricks, umu-launcher, icoutils, zenity, gamemode, mangohud, libvulkan1, mesa-vulkan-drivers, fonts-liberation, libnotify-bin, curl | wget, dosbox-x, python3-yaml, python3-hivex, udisks2
Suggests: bottles, lindos-gaming, vulkan-tools, ttf-mscorefonts-installer, gamescope, powershell
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos Windows-app compatibility layer (Wine / Proton via umu, recipes)
 Opens Windows programs and files on Lindos through Wine and Proton
 (umu-launcher) - a translation layer, not a virtual machine and not
 Windows.  Ships:
  * lindos-run     — double-click opener for every Windows file type:
                     programs and installers (.exe .msi .msp .bat .lnk),
                     packaged apps (.msix .appx, bundles, .appinstaller),
                     registry files (.reg, with a confirmation that lists
                     what they delete), scripts (.ps1 via PowerShell 7,
                     .vbs), Internet shortcuts (.url), screen savers,
                     Control Panel items, software .inf files, .cab
                     archives, disk images (.iso .img, AutoPlay-style
                     "Run setup?"), DOS programs (DOSBox-X) and 16-bit
                     Windows programs.  Every program gets its own C:\
                     drive (Wine prefix); what an installer created becomes
                     Start Menu entries and Lindos Settings > Windows apps
                     records.  Files that cannot work on Linux (drivers,
                     Windows updates, ARM-only programs, Store-encrypted or
                     UWP apps) are explained, never "tried anyway".
  * lindos-compat  — doctor (readiness check with fix commands), C:\ drive
                     management (list/remove/open/winecfg), honest recipes for
                     well-known programs (Photoshop CC 2021/CS6, Office 2016,
                     Notepad++, 7-Zip, ...), umu-launcher / Bottles installers,
                     Proton-GE via lindos-proton, file-type table, winget.
  * install-compat.sh — privileged installer (WineHQ staging for noble,
                     winetricks, 32-bit Vulkan/GL libs, umu-launcher) used by
                     the Lindos helper and the ISO build.
  * ./setup.exe in a terminal: the binfmt_misc rule lindos-pe
                     (/usr/lib/binfmt.d/lindos-pe.conf) hands Windows programs
                     to lindos-run; lindos-compat binfmt disable turns it off.
  * MIME types, defaults and Thunar actions ("Run with Lindos", "Run with
                     Proton", "Open C:\ drive", "Run with PowerShell",
                     "Install into a C:\ drive (MSIX)", "Mount disk image",
                     "Merge into a C:\ drive (.reg)").
 Anti-cheat titles (Valorant, League of Legends, Fortnite) do not run through
 Wine on any Linux today, so they are not supported on Lindos yet: that is up
 to their publishers and no date is given (Roblox's Windows client is blocked
 on Wine as well; Roblox itself works through Sober). lindos-run says so and
 points to 'lindos-game route <title>' (official cloud streaming where offered,
 or restarting into Windows) and to native alternatives.
